{"title": "Patient Consent", "body": "A Consent tab has been added to the patient profile, displaying the Consent that has or has not been provided in relation to their medical care. \n  Contents:\nWhere is the Consent Module\nCreating a Consent Record\nRemoving an Attachment from a Consent Record\nConsent Grid\nFiltering\nWhere is the Consent Module?\nNavigating to the Patient Record, within the tabs > select Consent.\nConsent can be recorded for all of the following:\nPrivacy policy \nProcedures and Operations \nTo send information, and correspondence to other providers and facilities \nOngoing Care after a patient has passed.\nFinancial Consent for upcoming costs \nCreating a Consent Record\nTo create a New Consent > select New Consent\nThere are six mandatory fields to be filled out when creating a New Consent.\nConsent By\nProvider\nStatus\nScope \nCategory \nStart date\nFields\nPatient (pre-filled from the current record).\nCreated date (prefilled from record creation).\nConsent By - Drop-down: Patient, Parent, Guardian, Other \nProvider - Consent provided to which person?\nStatus - Drop-down: Active, Draft, Entered in Error, Inactive, Proposed, Rejected.\nScope - General type of consent: Privacy, Treatment, Research, ADR (Advanced Directive).\nCategory - drop-down specific Consent type \nProvision - Yes / No - did the patient give consent for this? Declined consent should still be recorded against their Patient record.\nStart Date - Mandatory date field - determines the day that the consent starts.\nEnd Date - Non-Mandatory date field, can be used to show end-date if there is one, or left blank to show persisting (similar to the referral).\nFile upload - upload an attachment to consult up to 20 per record with maximum file of 20mb.\nComments - free text, enter any information required up to 500 characters.\n*NOTE: A consent cannot be deleted, you can however make it Inactive. \n  Removing an Attachment from a Consent Record\nThe user is also able to remove existing files from the consent record both in the \u2018File Upload\u2019 and \u2018Attachments\u2019 sections using the X icon beside the file. The file will only be removed once the Consent record has been saved. If the \u2018Cancel\u2019 button is pressed, the deletion of the file will not push through.\nFor files not yet saved in the consent record, the user can easily remove the file by clicking the X icon beside the file in the \u2018File Upload\u2019 section.\n\nFor already existing attachments to the consent record, clicking the X button will prompt a confirmation message for the user.\nClicking the Yes option will remove the file from the list.\nOnce the \u2018Save\u2019 button is clicked, it will be permanently removed from the consent record.\n    Consent Grid\nTo edit the consent - tick next to the consent on the left-hand side and click Edit.\nTo export - tick next to the consent and select Export\nA new column has been added to the Consent grid. Between the Status and Information columns, we have added the attachments column. Similar to the implementation in Consults, this column will indicate whether a specific consent record has attachments or not - if a paperclip icon is visible, then there is an attachment.\n\nWhen you hover over the paper clip icon, it will display a tooltip to inform the user that there is an attachment in the specific consent record and to view them, the consent record must be opened.\n    Filtering\nYou can filter the Grid by selecting the criteria you wish to define.\nProvider \nStatus\nScope \nCategory \nProvision\n     "}